 plans by September of 2015  the plans laid out how Trump Tower  Moscow would be a glass obelisk it would  be 100 stories tall with this sort of  diamond like shape at the top that if  you've been watching with us you saw in  the images we showed you already not  only were there plans the plans had also  been sent to the Russian develop their  developer that was engaged to actually  do the construction that's Andrew Roz  off he indicated he was ready to get  started on this project and there is  also as Rudy Giuliani did admit there is  this finalized letter of intent signed  by Donald Trump from about a month after  the architectural plans had been filed  and that includes that this building  would contain 250 luxury condos in the  tower 15 floors of hotel with 150 hotel  rooms there would be a spa there would  be a fitness center there would be a  commercial space as well as what is  called Class A office space in the  United States or more upscale luxury  type office space the letter of intent  even specifies that Donald Trump would  be paid 4 million bucks up front he  would then get 25% when the licensing  agreement is executed 25% when the  location is finalized and the other half  of that four million based on some other  milestones Trump would get a cut of  condo sales he would get a management  fee for 25 years he would get profit  sharing from the hotel and then after  all of that which already tells us it  wasn't just a nothing notion that Trump  wasn't at all involved in and that  nobody was taking seriously there were  architectural plans there were licensing  fees and future profit streams all laid  out there then we get to the gift to  Putin for going along with all of this  the top of the building was slated to  have a penthouse apartment the market  value would be roughly 50 million  dollars and as previously reported by  BuzzFeed news the plan was to give that  away for free to  Vladimir Putin just to have himself this  was not just an idea in a trump staffers  mind because two law enforcement  officials have confirmed that Michael  Cohen Trump's lawyer personally  discussed gifting the penthouse to  Vladimir Putin with an aide to Putin's  press secretary and it could have even  gone further than that we just aren't  sure yet this is what we call a bribe  okay Russian oligarch Felix seder who  was working with Trump on this and was a  key player in the Trump Russia probe is  on record saying quote my idea was to  give a 50 million dollar penthouse to  Putin and to charge 250 million more for  the rest of the units all the oleg arks  would line up to live in the same  building as Putin Seder was involved in  gifting the penthouse to Putin Michael  Cohen was involved in discussions about  that and aid to Putin's press secretary  was involved in that discussion and then  we get to the degree of involvement that  Donald Trump may or may not have had  Donald Trump has denied having any  interests in Russia he's denied being in  regular contact with anybody about this  project but BuzzFeed who did their  homework on this can now report that  Donald Trump received at least 10  updates about the project that they know  of specifically and of course in all of  this is the allegation that Trump  directed Michael Cohen to lie to  Congress about it on the basis of that  BuzzFeed news report from a few days ago  the cherry on top this tweet from Trump  in 2013 directed at Arras a gala Rove I  had a great weekend with you and your  family you have done a fantastic job  Trump Tower Moscow is next Amin was WOW  Ameen as I believe I Ross's son and was  involved in that  Trump Tower meeting that took place in  2016 so what's next it's going to be  what Rudy Giuliani's saying of course we  had plans it's a real estate deal you  need plans but so what making plans  isn't a crime licensing agreements  aren't crimes gifting penthouses to  presidents of foreign countries to get  deals approved that's not a crime this  is just business and then the next day  Rudy will tell us that was a  hypothetical statement that I made that  wasn't a legal statement I was  hypothetically quoting myself as Trump's  attorney but it was just hypothetical it  wasn't real and of course it would also  be wrong because there is this thing  called the Foreign Corrupt Practices Act  of 1977 it's also called FCPA  and it very specifically has anti bribe  provisions regarding using money or  things of value to influence or obtain  authorization for or promises from  foreign officials in their official  capacity so for everybody saying there's  nothing here this is merely a  businessman Trump trying to build a  tower that's not true there are a lot of  issues here it might violate the Foreign  Corrupt Practices Act it would be  indicative of the fact that Donald Trump  was not telling the truth about his  involvement here all along there are all  sorts of different crimes potentially  tied up in this the penthouse was a  thing of value offering it to Putin to  get an advantage in terms of permitting  and going forward with the project could  indeed be criminal and then lastly the  other potentially criminal element here  this project was set to receive funding  from the VTB Bank in Russia VTB Bank at  the time that these discussions were  going on was under sanctions by the  United States of America which makes the  financing of Trump Tower Moscow which we  now know did have architectural plans  it makes the fine the financing  potentially illegal as well so what will  they say will they say the BuzzFeed  report is simply wrong because every  time they do that BuzzFeed comes out  with more documents documentary evidence  about this will they say well Cohen  acted alone he's a liar and a convicted  felon does anybody believe for a moment  that Donald Trump would be not involved  in the plans to build the biggest  building in Europe including the gift of  a 50 million dollar penthouse to  Vladimir Putin when 9/11 happened Trump  went on TV and bragged as a result of  9/11 and  Twin Towers being knocked down his  building is now the tallest in lower  Manhattan does anybody believe that a  guy who does that that that's what he  thinks of when the twin towers are  knocked down by foreign terrorists does  anyone believe he wouldn't be involved  in the building of the tallest building  in Europe which was set to have his name  on it every single lie here is falling  apart let me know your thoughts i'm on  twitter at des Pakman and the show is on  twitter a David Pakman show

